3,Athabaskan-Eyak-Tlingit Languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/athabaskan-eyat-tlingit-languages/,Northern Athabaskan Isolates: Kwalhioqua-Clatskanie: extinct. Sarcee (alternate name: Tsuut’ina): 75 speakers according to UNESCO (2001) and 50 according to SIL (1995).,Tsúut’ínà,Eyak-Athabaskan
4,Athabaskan languages,https://www.translationdirectory.com/articles/article2550.php,"Athabaskan (also spelled Athabascan, Athapaskan or Athapascan, and also known as Dene) is a large family of indigenous languages of North America, located in western North America in three groups of contiguous languages: Northern, Pacific Coast and Southern (or Apachean).",Tsúut’ínà,Eyak-Athabaskan
